he Range of a Piecewise Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b6b62ba-3794-5abb-9e34-691ef037b3e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507686} {:answer/id #uuid "5d4a45a6-b31a-5201-8d1c-0356c0118a95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-2,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507734} {:answer/id #uuid "9d39011e-f888-5949-bb78-6ae4b979174b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507818} {:answer/id #uuid "b98ecbf9-4446-5930-82d3-f2c5edcdd2a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507855} {:answer/id #uuid "e44b6a95-a8a8-5f75-b737-edcd7a145fca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d39011e-f888-5949-bb78-6ae4b979174b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507818} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cc844ec-afa2-5997-a7b5-d632b50c4f9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a1d00aa5-c66d-5b2f-86d7-c93af95cd3b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-129503" :question/problem "![](images/1b/1b0b5c2160ca027b6acf752dfb4a31725d312b06e5c27127fcd66b7346eeee31.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "We find the ranges of the individual pieces, and then calculate their union:\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [-3,1]$ is $[-2,1]$\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in (1,3)$ is $(-3,1)$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $[-2,1]\\cup (-3,1)=(-3,1].$\n\n**Note:** From the graph, we see that the value $y=-3$ is NOT a valid output of the function $y=f(x).$ Therefore, we use parentheses $(…)$ instead of brackets $[…]$ at this endpoint."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508038 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ebb0209-904f-598a-9ff2-ab9d4d0cabca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Range of a Linear Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "362bbd4f-dc0b-5575-948f-250c8d55d8b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<f(x)\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507677} {:answer/id #uuid "3d59bda3-9d9d-5682-88c9-5757770ab9af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\le f(x)\\le \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507691} {:answer/id #uuid "4246f3be-f589-59ac-8ca0-e4c465f1e23b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<f(x)\\le \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507699} {:answer/id #uuid "e1d4c1d1-d753-57f3-80bf-d26501a1970a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<f(x)<3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507901} {:answer/id #uuid "ea75f889-1d7b-55b6-8ecc-891d4f5f1f1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<f(x)<\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4246f3be-f589-59ac-8ca0-e4c465f1e23b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<f(x)\\le \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507699} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ce85fa0-5910-5394-8fe4-97d58b71482a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "047624c0-9a25-551c-ac1f-663285e0168d" :question/math-academy-id "q-13724" :question/problem "Consider the linear function $f(x)=\\frac{x}{2},$ where $-2<x\\le 5.$ What is its range?" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/57/57f5c6e193c1db7dc05024088bdcae5cef890c252eb0c06621e36174e1353a0e.png)\n\nThen, we find the smallest and largest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The smallest $y$-value is $-1.$ This occurs at the point $(-2,-1).$ However, note that this point is not included in the graph.\n\n- The largest $y$-value is $\\frac{5}{2}.$ This occurs at the point $(5,\\frac{5}{2}).$\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-1$ and $\\frac{5}{2},$ including $\\frac{5}{2}$ but not including $-1.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-1<y\\le \\frac{5}{2},$ which can also be written as  \n\n$$\n-1<f(x)\\le \\frac{5}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179652 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d6727b20-2af5-5bff-aae4-e35c44fde144" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Range of a Piecewise Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "090f6b0d-954f-59b1-8627-6b16913c1f7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,-1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488493} {:answer/id #uuid "63672e31-cac6-5da3-a745-b0ce239264df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488661} {:answer/id #uuid "b22f6f36-3dde-51a4-a64b-073f992e2909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488825} {:answer/id #uuid "f9e00e11-d23c-50d4-bca3-793cebab7b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488997}] :