swer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f54c79d8-5b80-5135-8fbf-2f4df986e61d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cup " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488990} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9d5cf43-46d1-5177-8e2d-2002b8fcbaa2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "62541dad-de47-58c3-a80c-47be806ee721" :question/math-academy-id "q-235959" :question/problem "![](images/2d/2d46569e841a4bd7cf6646788f7bb5aec88a2386f96b8614ffec3e9c055bc200.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?\n\n$\\,$  The range is $f(x)\\in $\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "We find the ranges of the individual pieces, and then calculate their union:\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [-3,0)$ is $[0,2)$\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [0,3]$ is $[-3,-1]$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $[-3,-1]\\cup [0,2).$\n\n**Note:** From the graph, we see that the value $y=2$ is NOT a valid output of the function $y=f(x).$ Therefore, we use parentheses $(…)$ instead of brackets $[…]$ at this endpoint."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508051 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ebb0209-904f-598a-9ff2-ab9d4d0cabca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Range of a Linear Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d29ce9dc-0d54-5390-8011-2f6b0d6f9a8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d29ce9dc-0d54-5390-8011-2f6b0d6f9a8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507888} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c7aa346-9a6e-5089-87c4-e81ec7b7d494" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507974} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfac7788-3b58-5927-a4db-53ffa93ced79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfac7788-3b58-5927-a4db-53ffa93ced79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507900} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cda5acf-1a37-58b4-b47d-d804b006db0e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507975} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b04ac51-3506-5813-bf0d-4f7b035f6391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b04ac51-3506-5813-bf0d-4f7b035f6391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507711} :answer-field/id #uuid "c61573f5-b18b-5585-9962-5cb9203f87fd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1bd1c83e-29b0-58c6-bbc9-6066b2370a02" :question/math-academy-id "q-235981" :question/problem "Consider the linear function $f(x)=\\frac{x}{2}-1,$ where $x$ is any real number. What is its range?\n\nThe range is \n{{field-1}}\n\n$<f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/de/de9f7bcc43c626c12da1dde90660c0a231bb6ad9320b8e2c08cfbd1241d034d0.png)\n\nThe graph will cover all $y$-values, so the range of the function is $-\\infty <y<\\infty ,$ which can also be written as\n\n$$\n-\\infty <f(x)<\\infty .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179651 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6df7104d-0f74-5301-9525-132c74c19ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Range of a Function by Considering Its End Behavior"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3e2fe1e-5ce8-5259-883a-e27ba55b0ebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3e2fe1e-5ce8-5259-883a-e27ba55b0ebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489908} :answer-field/id #uuid "2356dd8e-95af-53aa-99c1-588dd0a4fe73" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490089} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42a84cca-e35f-5c4a-b07e-845a7d28433f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42a84cca-e35f-5c4a-b07e-845a7d28433f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489667} :answer-field/id #uuid "3443567b-7d91-5f03-9d4e-6b2b217a9066" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490103} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80e903e5-f2b3-5ed4-a09b-70f4dda6a048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80e903e5-f2b3-5ed4-a09b-70f4dda6a048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489807} :answer-field/id #uuid "9abeb5f8-371d-515e-a1f6-7daf65af6f1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c426db9-03a0-51ed-9522-bdc02ff647af" :question/math-academy-id "q-236388" :question/problem "![](images/49/49288e2c082854cfc27a2d48af2d82a96016a3c1394066471d49873e4c75878e.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?\n\nThe range is \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)<$\n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the smallest and largest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The smallest $y$-value is $1.$ This occurs when $x=0.$\n\n- There is no largest $y$-value.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $1$ and $\\infty ,$ including $1.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $1\\le y<\\infty ,$ which can also be written as \n$1\\le f(x)<\\infty .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179651 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6df7104d-0f74-5301-9525-132c74c19ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Range of a Function by Considering Its End Behavior"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "077fd3b6-a66f-5992-89ff-f734285036e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1<f(x)<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489533} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd4f26c-68d7-508b-ae68-df55769b27e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty <f(x)<1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489797} {:answer/id #uuid "85a2736a-d41e-5e05-9a88-0d47451e0a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1<f(x)<\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489820} {:answer/id #uuid "a7ab8a0a-f5d1-5b79-8ad9-de72a82f973b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty <f(x)\\le 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489884} {:answer/id #uuid "c20f2f3c-997e-5379-8c75-90a1c8d674a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\le f(x)<\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bd4f26c-68d7-508b-ae68-df55769b27e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty <f(x)<1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489797} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7dd7694-ccde-505f-9224-5e793348c4a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24be045a-a1e0-562b-a001-f17a0f6f12b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-79997" :question/problem "![](images/ac/acbf4ae592e7912e6e27415ce99f872c4c0ec1737cfa3269635f37f7fa0fe5db.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the smallest and largest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- There is no smallest $y$-value.\n\n- The largest $y$-value is $1.$ This occurs when $x\\to -\\infty .$ However, note that this point is not included in the graph.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-\\infty $ and $1,$ but not including $1.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-\\infty <y<1,$ which can also be written as  $-\\infty <f(x)<1.$"}]}
